{"type": "tool_call", "n": 23, "ts": 1790150059.1788008, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "MEMO \u2013 Q1 2026 board deck vs GL: US Software Subscriptions (GL 6200)\nPrepared by: senior accountant (david.murguia@gmail.com), 2026-04-03. No entries posted.\n\n1. THE NUMBERS\n- Board deck, Appendix B (DOC-0207), prepared by FP&A from the GL as of 2026-04-01 09:00: USD 11,769.00\n- GL 6200 US today: Jan 4,289.70 + Feb 4,139.80 + Mar 6,139.50 = USD 14,569.00\n- Difference: USD 2,800.00\n\n2. WHAT EXPLAINS THE DIFFERENCE (fully reconciled)\nThe entire 2,800.00 is one entry: JE-00304, \"Tessellate BI \u2013 TB-Q1-TRUEUP \u2013 Q1 seat true-up\", Dr 6200 / Cr 2000 AP, dated 2026-03-31. It was created by ap.clerk at 2026-04-02 10:14 \u2014 roughly 25 hours after FP&A took the GL snapshot \u2014 and back-dated into March. Support: vendor invoice DOC-0206 (Tessellate BI, invoice date 2026-03-31, \"Q1 2026 seat true-up, 14 additional seats, Jan\u2013Mar\", USD 2,800.00). The service relates to Q1, so the expense belongs in Q1 and the GL treatment is correct. The deck is simply stale; there is no error in the ledger for this item.\n\nDeck tie-out: 14,569.00 \u2212 2,800.00 = 11,769.00 = deck figure. No other Q1 6200 entry was created after 2026-04-01 09:00.\n\n3. OTHER ITEMS REVIEWED (not part of the difference)\na) Two Zoom card charges on 2026-03-08 (JE-00247 and JE-00248, 149.90 each). Checked against the March bank statement: two separate debits exist (BT-US-0062 and BT-US-0063), each with its own receipt (DOC-0173, DOC-0174). This is not a duplicate GL posting and both were in the deck snapshot. If Zoom double-charged the card, that is a vendor refund question, not a ledger correction.\nb) Figtree annual license amortization for March 2026 (USD 1,250.00) has NOT yet been booked. Schedule DOC-0067 shows Jan and Feb booked (JE-00108, JE-00204) and \"Mar-2026: to be booked at March close\"; checklist item \"Amortize prepaid software\" is still open. Per instruction I did not post it; flagged as an exception for controller action.\n\n4. CORRECT Q1 FIGURE\n- As the GL stands today: USD 14,569.00 (deck should be updated from 11,769.00 to at least this).\n- Once the March Figtree amortization is booked as scheduled: USD 15,819.00. This is the figure the deck should show for Q1 US Software Subscriptions at final close.\nQ1 composition at 15,819.00: Tessellate BI 3 \u00d7 1,950 + 2,800 true-up = 8,650.00; Quire Docs 3 \u00d7 640 = 1,920.00; Zoom 11 \u00d7 149.90 = 1,648.90 (Jan 3, Feb 2, Mar 6 incl. the two on 03-08); Figtree amortization 3 \u00d7 1,250 = 3,750.00; not matching to cents: 8,650 + 1,920 + 1,648.90 + 3,750 = 15,968.90 \u2014 note: correct Zoom count is 10 charges (Jan 3, Feb 2, Mar 5): 1,499.00. Recomputed: 8,650.00 + 1,920.00 + 1,499.00 + 3,750.00 = 15,819.00. Ties.\n\n5. RECOMMENDATIONS\n- FP&A to re-pull Appendix B after the March close is complete rather than from a mid-close snapshot, and to note the snapshot timestamp on the page.\n- Controller to book the March Figtree amortization (open checklist item) before the deck is refreshed."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 9}
